3. The Breakthrough Moment
Everything changed when I stopped watching tutorials and started building.

Before the breakthrough:
Watched 50+ hours of YouTube tutorials

Could understand code but couldn't write it

Felt like I was learning but not progressing

After the breakthrough:
Started building a simple calculator

Got stuck every 5 minutes

Googled errors constantly

But after 3 days, I had a working program

python
# My first real project (simple calculator)
def calculator():
    num1 = float(input("Enter first number: "))
    op = input("Enter operator (+, -, *, /): ")
    num2 = float(input("Enter second number: "))
    
    if op == '+':
        print(f"Result: {num1 + num2}")
    elif op == '-':
        print(f"Result: {num1 - num2}")
    elif op == '*':
        print(f"Result: {num1 * num2}")
    elif op == '/':
        print(f"Result: {num1 / num2}")
    else:
        print("Invalid operator")

calculator()
The breakthrough: I realized that struggling = learning. Every error fixed was a lesson learned.

