6. Mistakes I Made (So You Don't Have To)
❌ Mistake #1: Watching too many tutorials
What I did: Watched 10 different "Python for Beginners" courses

What I should have done: Watched 1 course, then built something

The fix: 20% learning, 80% doing

❌ Mistake #2: Not using Git/GitHub from day 1
What I did: Kept all my code on my local computer

What I should have done: Put everything on GitHub

The fix: Create a GitHub account and push every single project

❌ Mistake #3: Comparing myself to others
What I did: Saw experts on Twitter and felt behind

What I should have done: Focus on my own progress

The fix: Delete social media apps during learning time

❌ Mistake #4: Trying to learn everything
What I did: Jumped between web dev, data science, AI, game dev

What I should have done: Mastered one area first

The fix: Pick ONE path and stick with it for 3 months

❌ Mistake #5: Not building a portfolio
What I did: Learned for 3 months without showing anyone

What I should have done: Share progress daily/weekly

The fix: Post your code on GitHub, Twitter, LinkedIn

