8. How I Started Teaching Python
Here's something unexpected: The best way to learn is to teach.

How I started teaching:
Wrote my first tutorial (on LinkedIn — got 500+ views)

Created my GitHub course (structured lessons + exercises)

Answered questions on forums (helped me identify gaps)

Recorded short videos (forced me to explain clearly)

What teaching gave me:
Deeper understanding of concepts

Confidence in my skills

A portfolio that stands out

Connections with other developers

Job opportunities (yes, really)

python
# The teaching mindset
def learn_by_teaching(topic):
    understand = learn(topic)
    explain = teach(topic)
    
    if explain:
        return "You truly understand it"
    else:
        return "Time to review"
